From 3b2977eb796dac0956087701db669dba2f4a5635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reshke <reshke@double.cloud>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:52:32 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add pg_manage_prepared_xacts for transaction managers

An external transaction manager may need to resolve transactions prepared
by different application users after the original connections disappear.
Requiring the preparing user or a superuser forces a dedicated recovery
login to impersonate each application role or obtain superuser privileges.

Add a predefined pg_manage_prepared_xacts role whose privileges allow
COMMIT PREPARED and ROLLBACK PREPARED for any owner, including superusers.
Use normal inherited-role privileges, leaving the exact-owner rule intact
for callers without the management privilege. The existing same-database
restriction continues to apply. Check role membership before acquiring
TwoPhaseStateLock so catalog access is outside the shared-memory lock.

The original owner/superuser policy was proposed in the 2004 two-phase
commit discussion. The exact OID comparison was explicitly left unchanged
when role membership support was discussed in 2005. An explicit management
role provides delegation without changing implicit ownership semantics.

Document the role and both commands, bump the catalog version for the new
initial role, and cover inheritance, non-inherited grants, SET ROLE,
revocation, owner and superuser behavior in regression tests. Add recovery
coverage with a separate management login, including clean restart, crash
recovery, and rejection from the wrong database.

Validation: assertion-enabled build; all 239 regression tests and 45 TAP
assertions in 009_twophase and 061_manage_prepared_xacts passed.

Discussion: https://www.postgresql.org/message-id/15495.1097685302@sss.pgh.pa.us
Discussion: https://www.postgresql.org/message-id/26627.1119985659@sss.pgh.pa.us
